WEBVTT

1
00:00:10.400 --> 00:00:19.246
Mother Wolf gazed at the small human in wonder.

2
00:00:19.246 --> 00:00:23.181
"He's so little!" she said softly.

3
00:00:23.181 --> 00:00:28.516
The young boy was squirming between two cubs to get warm.

4
00:00:28.516 --> 00:00:32.770
"Look at that! He's not afraid of us or the cubs."

5
00:00:32.770 --> 00:00:38.195
"I've heard of young humans living with wolves," Father Wolf said.

6
00:00:38.195 --> 00:00:42.032
"But I've never seen it in my own pack."

7
00:00:42.032 --> 00:00:47.904
Just then the wolves heard something and spun toward the entrance of the cave.

8
00:00:47.904 --> 00:00:52.930
Tabaqui had returned—with the tiger, Shere Khan.

9
00:00:52.930 --> 00:01:02.421
"The boy is here, master!" the jackal said eagerly. "I see him."

10
00:01:02.421 --> 00:01:09.317
"Shere Khan, your visit brings us great honor," Father Wolf said politely.

11
00:01:09.317 --> 00:01:15.380
But his eyes sparked with anger. "What do you need?"

12
00:01:15.380 --> 00:01:20.119
"A human cub went this way," Shere Khan said.

13
00:01:20.119 --> 00:01:26.494
"His parents have run off. Give the man cub to me."

14
00:01:26.494 --> 00:01:32.149
Luckily, the cave entrance was too narrow for Shere Khan to enter.

15
00:01:32.149 --> 00:01:37.197
"We wolves are free creatures," said Father Wolf.

16
00:01:37.197 --> 00:01:41.833
"We take orders from the head of the pack, not from you."

17
00:01:41.833 --> 00:01:48.183
The tiger's furious roar filled the cave.

18
00:01:48.183 --> 00:01:51.775
Mother Wolf sprang forward.

19
00:01:51.775 --> 00:01:58.101
In the darkness her eyes looked like two green moons as she faced Shere Khan.

20
00:01:58.101 --> 00:02:01.819
"The human cub is mine!" She growled.

21
00:02:01.819 --> 00:02:03.976
"He will not be killed.

22
00:02:03.976 --> 00:02:07.617
He will live to run with the pack and to hunt with the pack.

23
00:02:07.617 --> 00:02:11.048
Now go, Shere Khan!"

24
00:02:11.048 --> 00:02:14.023
Father looked on in amazement.

25
00:02:14.023 --> 00:02:19.060
He had forgotten how fierce his mate could be when she was angry.

26
00:02:19.060 --> 00:02:22.306
Shere Khan backed away from the cave.

27
00:02:22.306 --> 00:02:28.725
"We'll see what the pack says about that human cub!" He snarled.

28
00:02:28.725 --> 00:02:40.003
"He's mine, and his life will end in my teeth!"

29
00:02:40.003 --> 00:02:47.472
Mother threw herself down among the cubs as Father watched the tiger stalk off.

30
00:02:47.472 --> 00:02:56.260
"Shere Khan spoke the truth about one thing," Father said with a sigh.

31
00:02:56.260 --> 00:02:59.294
"We must show this cub to the pack.

32
00:02:59.294 --> 00:03:02.488
Do you really plan to keep him?"

33
00:03:02.488 --> 00:03:06.129
"Of course I'll keep him!" Mother snapped.

34
00:03:06.129 --> 00:03:10.774
"The poor little creature came at night, alone and hungry.

35
00:03:10.775 --> 00:03:14.164
I'll call him Mowgli," she added.

36
00:03:14.164 --> 00:03:20.274
"One day he will hunt Shere Khan, just as that tiger has hunted him."

37
00:03:20.274 --> 00:03:24.852
Father was worried. "What will our pack say?"

38
00:03:24.853 --> 00:03:30.261
The law of the jungle was very clear.

39
00:03:30.261 --> 00:03:37.304
The pack protected young cubs until they were old enough to hunt on their own.

40
00:03:37.304 --> 00:03:41.736
But the pack wasn't likely to protect a human cub.

41
00:03:41.736 --> 00:03:46.323
"We'll deal with that later," Mother replied firmly.

42
00:03:46.323 --> 00:03:50.871
The pack council met once every month, when the moon was full.

43
00:03:50.872 --> 00:03:57.321
It was the duty of all new parents to show their cubs to the council.

44
00:03:57.321 --> 00:04:03.405
On the night of the next pack meeting, Father and Mother went to Council Rock.

45
00:04:03.405 --> 00:04:09.650
The wolf cubs and Mowgli ran after them.

46
00:04:09.650 --> 00:04:14.974
Council Rock was a hilltop covered with stones and boulders.

47
00:04:14.974 --> 00:04:20.033
Akela, the great gray wolf, lay across a rock.

48
00:04:20.033 --> 00:04:23.341
He had led the pack for a year now.

49
00:04:23.341 --> 00:04:29.143
He was a wise, strong leader, who knew the ways and customs of people.

50
00:04:29.144 --> 00:04:35.335
It was very quiet at Council Rock. All the parents sat in a circle.

51
00:04:35.335 --> 00:04:40.775
In the center of the circle, the cubs tumbled over one another, playing.

52
00:04:40.775 --> 00:04:46.670
One by one, the wolf parents showed their cubs to show the pack.

53
00:04:46.670 --> 00:04:51.835
"Look well, oh, wolves!" Akela cried.

54
00:04:51.836 --> 00:04:54.773
The mothers anxiously repeated the call.

55
00:04:54.773 --> 00:05:00.838
"Look, look well, oh, wolves!"

56
00:05:00.838 --> 00:05:03.034
Mother's fur quivered.

57
00:05:03.034 --> 00:05:06.735
It was almost time to show Mowgli to the pack.

58
00:05:06.735 --> 00:05:16.587
What would the wolves say when they saw the odd-looking man cub?
